
$ NASTRAN Input File: Flat Plate Free-Free Modal Analysis
$ Dimensions: 100mm x 300mm x 1mm
$ Material: Steel (Iron properties)
$ Units: mm, N, Tonne, MPa

ID PLATE, MODES
SOL 103                 $ Modal analysis solution sequence
TIME 10
CEND

TITLE = Free-Free Modal Analysis of a Rectangular Plate
METHOD = 10             $ Refer to EIGRL card below
ECHO = NONE
DISPLACEMENT = ALL

BEGIN BULK


$ --- Eigenvalue Extraction (Extract the first 10 modes) ---
$      ID      V1      V2      ND
EIGRL   10                      10      MAX

 
$ --- Geometric Points (GRID) ---
$ Divide into a simple 3x9 grid (100/33.3 x 300/33.3)
GRID    1               0.0     0.0     0.0
GRID    2               50.0    0.0     0.0
GRID    3               100.0   0.0     0.0
GRID    4               0.0     150.0   0.0
GRID    5               50.0    150.0   0.0
GRID    6               100.0   150.0   0.0
GRID    7               0.0     300.0   0.0
GRID    8               50.0    300.0   10.
GRID    9               100.0   300.0   0.0


$ --- Element Definition (CQUAD4) ---
$      EID     PID     G1      G2      G3      G4
CQUAD4  1       1       1       2       5       4
CQUAD4  2       1       2       3       6       5
CQUAD4  3       1       4       5       8       7
CQUAD4  4       1       5       6       9       8


$ --- Property Definition (PSHELL) ---
$      PID     MID     T
PSHELL  1       100     1.0


$ --- Material Definition (MAT1) Iron/Steel ---
$ Units: Length mm, Mass Tonne, Time s, Force N
$ Young's modulus E=2.1E5 MPa, Poisson's ratio nu=0.3, Density rho=7.8E-9 T/mm^3
$      MID     E       G       NU      RHO
MAT1    100     2.1E5           0.3     7.8E-9

ENDDATA